✗ controller registers nothing

    module "greeter" (warren/module.go:14)
      └─ warren.Controllers lists a constructor returning *warren_test.silentController,
           which has no Register(transport.Registrar) method.

  A controller whose Register has the wrong signature compiles, registers
  no routes, and 404s in production. Add:

      func (c *silentController) Register(r transport.Registrar) {
          transport.Post(r, "/things", c.create)
      }

  Or, if it registers nothing and only needs building at boot, declare it
  with warren.Providers and warren.Eager[*warren_test.silentController]() instead.